  abstract = {Objective To compare the diagnostic value of standard DR,tissue equalization(TE) and CT in thoracolumbar vertebral fractures.Methods 60 cases were randomly selected from among patients confirmed with thoracolumbar vertebral fractures by orthopedic surgery from January 2008 to September 2011.All patients had trauma history.In the picture archiving and communication system(PACS),preoperative images including DR thoracolumbar plain films(anteroposterior,lateral and former oblique),DR TE images and thoracolumbar CT of the 60 patients were collected.The detection of fracture,fracture sites and accompanied symptoms were comparatively analyzed and the diagnosis results were recorded by four experienced doctors by using double-blind method.Results(1)There were a total of 107 fractures in the 60 patients.Standard DR images detected 96 fractures(89.7%),DR TE images detected 105 fractures(98.1%) and CT images detected 101 fractures(94.4%).The difference of detection rate between the three methods showed statistically significant difference(P0.05).The detection rate of DR TE images was significantly higher than standard DR images(P0.01).(2)As for vertebral fractures,standard DR images,DR TE images and CT images detected 45(88.2%),51(100.0%) and 46(90.2%) fractures respectively,and the difference was statistically significant(P0.05).The detection rate of DR TE images on vertebral fractures was significantly higher than standard DR images and CT images(P0.05).(3)As for the fracture fragmen},
}

